b76155e-39de-4952-857b-bf53a1586810", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[Milan](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1015) has used an executable named `companycatalog.exe.config` to appear benign.(Citation: ClearSky Siamesekitten August 2021)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004761904761904762, "relevance_grade": 0.004761904761904762}, {"doc_id": "relationship--fce88056-31db-43be-be76-fb1aaf076ed1", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096) has created services to appear as benign system tools.(Citation: Group IB APT 41 June 2021)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004687500000000001, "relevance_grade": 0.004687500000000001}, {"doc_id": "relationship--3922a8b2-5a5d-4822-be22-75f246d56fa4", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[RainyDay](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0629) has named services and scheduled tasks to appear benign including \"ChromeCheck\" and \"googleupdate.\"(Citation: Bitdefender Naikon April 2021)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004615384615384616, "relevance_grade": 0.004615384615384616}, {"doc_id": "relationship--60692cc5-ca97-4c1d-8011-8dbe111ca8f4", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[DEADWOOD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1134) will attempt to masquerade its service execution using benign-looking names such as <code>ScDeviceEnums</code>.(Citation: SentinelOne Agrius 2021)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004545454545454546, "relevance_grade": 0.004545454545454546}, {"doc_id": "relationship--67e631d1-439f-4630-9662-8ea74ab10234", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[Brute Ratel C4](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1063) has used a payload file named OneDrive.update to appear benign.(Citation: Palo Alto Brute Ratel July 2022)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004477611940298508, "relevance_grade": 0.004477611940298508}, {"doc_id": "relationship--d7e049fb-ac90-4e93-8907-eca54ba04ebd", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\nThe [NETWIRE](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0198) payload has been injected into benign Microsoft executables via process hollowing.(Citation: FireEye NETWIRE March 2019)(Citation: Red Canary NETWIRE January 2020)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004411764705882354, "relevance_grade": 0.004411764705882354}, {"doc_id": "relationship--2447ac98-019d-40a9-8913-c97d6eb93d90", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[Kimsuky](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0094) has disguised services to appear as benign software or related to operating system functions.(Citation: CISA AA20-301A Kimsuky)(Citation: Securonix Kimsuky February 2025)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004347826086956523, "relevance_grade": 0.004347826086956523}, {"doc_id": "relationship--ea99ff52-af1e-49af-9cfe-b224c9a9eea4", "title": "Relationship: ", "content": "****\n\n[RCSession](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0662) has used a file named English.rtf to appear benign on victim hosts.(Citation: Secureworks BRONZE PRESIDENT December 2019)(Citation: Trend Micro DRBControl February 2020)", "source": "mitre-attack-stix", "provenance_status": "VALID", "sanitization_status": "SANITIZED", "conflict_status": "NONE", "score": 0.004285714285714286, "relevance_grade": 0.004285714285714286}], "trace